1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.900
The Client Catcher, a real run.
Never lose a lead.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.400
A front desk dashboard opens on Today.
Suds and Shine Mobile Detailing, a worked example.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.500
While Maya is with a client, nothing slips.
Every missed call, form fill and message gets caught.

4
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.000
Three counters: 34 leads caught,
a 28 second first reply, 21 booked.

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.000
A notice slides in. A missed call from a customer.
Maya is with a client. An instant text-back goes out.

6
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.500
Step one, catch. The lead inbox lists four
new leads with where each one came from.

7
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Each lead is scored on intent, timing and value.
Jasmine, a missed call, scores highest.

8
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Step two, follow up, in the owner's own voice.
A reply is being written back to Jasmine.

9
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.000
The reply apologises for the missed call,
explains she was mid-appointment, and offers the week.

10
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.400
Jasmine answers and asks about Thursday.
A booking link goes back to her.

11
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.000
Step three, book. Her own screen opens
on a live booking page with four times on it.

12
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.200
She picks ten in the morning
and confirms it herself.

13
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.400
Back in the thread, Jasmine confirms.
A reminder is promised for Wednesday night.

14
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.500
Nobody at the business has touched
the conversation yet.

15
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.500
The calendar opens. Thursday the 23rd
now carries a full service booking.

16
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.800
Booked. Caught, followed up and booked
in 43 seconds, with no taps from the owner.

17
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.300
Back on Today, the counters have moved.
35 caught, 22 on the calendar.

18
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.450
Live in 7 days. Booking in 30.
Or you don't pay. frimpomaasync.com
